# {{ .APP_NAME }}

A Svelte 5 + Vite + TypeScript app that opens a SpeechKit Voice Agent
WebSocket session and exchanges typed turns. The frame protocol matches
[asyncapi.v1.yaml](https://speechkit.cc/api/asyncapi.v1.yaml).

This template is a **text-first** baseline. Mic capture and audio
playback are intentionally out of scope so the protocol is easy to read;
upgrade with [`@speechkit/voiceagent-client`](https://speechkit.cc) when
the dedicated browser/Node SDK package ships.

## Prerequisites

- Node 20+
- A running SpeechKit Server with Voice Agent enabled (default `{{ .SPEECHKIT_SERVER_URL }}`)
- (optional) Bearer token for `auth_mode = "bearer"` deployments

## Configure

```sh
cp .env.example .env
# adjust VITE_SPEECHKIT_SERVER_URL, VITE_SPEECHKIT_TOKEN, VITE_SPEECHKIT_PERSONA_ID
```

## Run

```sh
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open <http://localhost:5173>, click **Connect**, and type to send a
user-turn. The agent's transcribed replies appear in the log; binary
audio frames are received but skipped (browser audio playback is the
follow-up task).

## How it works

1. `voiceagent.ts.tmpl` POSTs to `/v1/voiceagent/sessions` to mint a
   `session_id` + `ticket`.
2. It opens `WS /v1/voiceagent/sessions/{id}/ws?ticket=...`.
3. Sends a `start` frame with the persona id.
4. Dispatches incoming `state`, `input_transcript`, `output_transcript`,
   `tool_call`, `error`, and `session_end` frames.

To register a custom tool, pass it via `openSession({ tools: { ... } })`.
The handler signature is
`(call: { id, name, args }) => Promise<Record<string, unknown>>`.
